 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425323 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425323 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "52ba5050-79f5-5038-b180-5f46df5f54fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425329 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b2adb06a-393f-5309-9bba-b9aeaa0795a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425332 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ed34ebf7-d0c0-5560-bc6c-feaad1d7a4a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.\n\n$\\,$ The equilibrium point (origin) is a \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\nnode." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6510dfcd-a99e-5730-8a08-a25b49094096" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425334 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix of our system is\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- Since the only (repeated) eigenvalue of $A$ is $\\lambda =3$ and it's positive, we have a $\\text{unstable}$ node.\n\n- Since $A$ is diagonal and has a repeated eigenvalue, there are infinitely many linearly independent eigenvectors. So, we have a $\\text{star}$ node.\n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/95/95bb5be106524711e86d2e1ff9cb21d61141c25eb0a2f8958b51c29791806ccc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186425335 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425335 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425335 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425335 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186425335 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9addc7f5-7ff7-5987-87ac-e05cc5e87102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425335 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=7$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{7t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/71/71b5e685e876b0e7e33a3db5e1edc3579730d179867fe3b17b05574942201181.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186425336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425336 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425336 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425336 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186425336 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c87fc503-31b5-5d30-8770-67dd20112235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425336 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{-3t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/bf/bffb2f815cc5a7db0c521054006aa834b17071f5dd33a97fe977e5d118b771be.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186478476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186478488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186478490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1045 "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Repeated Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186478476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477732 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "cacf7310-3c00-5589-9153-aa9a4d046b77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477737 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477737 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477737 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "024e08bd-5d19-54df-95c6-50e41bb1a673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477743 #edb/ref 1080 "\\infty " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477743 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477743 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0415064c